{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan an Nasai","name_native":"Sunan an-Nasa'i","section":{"13":"The Book of Forgetfulness (In Prayer)"},"section_detail":{"13":{"hadithnumber_first":1179,"hadithnumber_last":1366,"arabicnumber_first":1179,"arabicnumber_last":1366,"name_native":"Livre de la prière (Salat)"}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":1276,"arabicnumber":1276,"text":"Rapporté par Abu Hurairah : Le Messager d'Allah (ﷺ) a dit : \"Les gens doivent absolument arrêter de lever les yeux vers le ciel lorsqu'ils invoquent pendant la prière, sinon ils perdront la vue","grades":[{"name":"Abu Ghuddah","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}],"reference":{"book":13,"hadith":98}}]}